# `actuarial::Triangle::observed`

[Back to `actuarial::Triangle`](../Triangle.md)

The mask of observed cells.

## Signature

```cpp
const pluss::Series &actuarial::Triangle::observed() const noexcept;
```

## What It Does

Returns the `norigins × ndevelopment` boolean matrix that is true where a cell holds data. Observed cells are left-contiguous in every row, so the number of observed cells in row `i` is the development age reached by origin `i`. When the triangle was built without a mask, a cell is observed if it is positive; give a mask to [`cumulative`](../cumulative.md) when a genuine observed amount can be zero.

## Returns

A const reference to a two-dimensional boolean `Series`; undefined for an undefined triangle.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1: the staircase

Ones where there is data.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(0));
  const pluss::Series cumulative = pluss::make_series({100.0, 180.0, 220.0, 240.0,
                                                       110.0, 200.0, 250.0, 0.0,
                                                       120.0, 215.0, 0.0, 0.0,
                                                       130.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0}, {4, 4});
  const actuarial::Triangle triangle = actuarial::triangle::cumulative(cumulative);
  const auto o = triangle.observed().reshape({16}).items<double>();
  for (int r = 0; r < 4; ++r) out.writeln(o[4*r], o[4*r+1], o[4*r+2], o[4*r+3]);
}
```

### Example 2: the age reached by each origin

The row sums of the mask.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(0));
  const pluss::Series cumulative = pluss::make_series({100.0, 180.0, 220.0, 240.0,
                                                       110.0, 200.0, 250.0, 0.0,
                                                       120.0, 215.0, 0.0, 0.0,
                                                       130.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0}, {4, 4});
  const actuarial::Triangle triangle = actuarial::triangle::cumulative(cumulative);
  out.writeln(triangle.observed().sum(1).items<double>());
}
```

### Example 3: an explicit mask

A genuine zero is kept as an observed cell when the mask says so.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(0));
  const pluss::Series values = pluss::make_series({0.0, 10.0, 5.0, 0.0}, {2, 2});
  const pluss::Series mask = pluss::make_series({1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 0.0}, {2, 2}).gt(0.5);
  const actuarial::Triangle t = actuarial::triangle::cumulative(values, mask);
  out.writeln("observed =", t.observed().reshape({4}).items<double>());
}
```

### Example 4: without a mask, zero means unobserved

The same values without a mask: the leading zero makes the first row non-contiguous and is refused.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const auto report = [&](const auto &call) {
    try {
      call();
    } catch (const std::exception &e) {
      std::string text(e.what());
      if (const auto cut = text.find("Triggered"); cut != std::string::npos) text.erase(cut);
      while (!text.empty() && text.back() == '\n') text.pop_back();
      out.writeln(text);
    }
  };
  report([&] { (void)actuarial::triangle::cumulative(pluss::make_series({0.0, 10.0, 5.0, 0.0}, {2, 2})); });
}
```

